{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And he removed on that day the streaked and the spotted he-goats.</b> Which he interpreted as the speckled and the brindled:" "<b>The speckled females and the spotted females.</b> He interpreted as the streaked females and the brindled females, and this is the meaning of \"every one that is Laban's in it,\"" "And every dark sheep, a black lamb, and it is an adjective, like פָּעוֹל, and its pattern is like \"סוּג לֵב\" (Proverbs 14:14). And the word הָסֵר there, according to a great grammarian, is the verb לְהָסִיר with the meaning \"remove from there,\" and these are my wages. And he interpreted \"and he gave into the hand of his sons\" — the sons of Jacob — but \"only he set a distance of three days\" refers to Laban himself. But this interpretation is not correct, for Jacob has no son older than Reuben, and furthermore he has not yet completed seven years. And so he interpreted the verse: הַסֵּר מִשָּׁם in its literal sense as an imperative, and the meaning of \"and it shall be my wages\" is: after you remove such ones from there." "<b>And my righteousness shall answer for me.</b> Before you it will testify, when you come and see my wages — that is, the flock that I set aside for myself — if you do not find the he-goats and the goats streaked, speckled, and brindled, and the sheep black, stolen with me. For behold, you yourself removed from the flock every streaked and speckled and brindled among the goats, and every dark one among the sheep:" "<b>And Laban said, Hen.</b> Like הֵן, for the heh is added, like הָאֵלֶּה הָאֵל:" "<b>And he removed on that day.</b> Laban removed:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "The referents of 'he interpreted' and 'the great grammarian' are uncertain; likely a prior exegete such as Rashi or the Gaon [Saadia]. The parsing of the second half involves uncertain clause divisions; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:34.794704571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}